trace.request:
Administer 100% oxygen via hood or CPAP for 10 minutes, then measure arterial PaO₂ (or preductal SpO₂ if arterial blood gas unavailable); interpret:  
- PaO₂ >100 mmHg or SpO₂ >95% suggests pulmonary disease (e.g., RDS);  
- PaO₂ <100 mmHg or SpO₂ <90% despite 100% O₂ suggests significant right-to-left shunting (e.g., CHD).

